Test startup checks for the webhook token and the updates path

`python -m pihub` with a webhook token under 32 characters, or a file:
reference to a missing file, exits with code 2 and does not log the token;
new tests run it as a subprocess. Where updates are saved moved into
updates_path() (PIHUB_UPDATES, else updates.json next to the config) so it
is tested. The server docstring now says dismissing works whenever updates
are kept, while only the webhook needs PIHUB_WEBHOOK_TOKEN.

Files: pihub/updates.py, pihub/__main__.py, pihub/server.py,
tests/test_updates.py, tests/test_main.py
